# Title: Potential Suspicious Windows Feature Enabled - ProcCreation
# ID: c740d4cf-a1e9-41de-bb16-8a46a4f57918
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-12-29
# Tags: attack.stealth
# Description: Detects usage of the built-in PowerShell cmdlet "Enable-WindowsOptionalFeature" used as a Deployment Image Servicing and Management tool.
# Similar to DISM.exe, this cmdlet is used to enumerate, install, uninstall, configure, and update features and packages in Windows images
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((cmdline:*Enable-WindowsOptionalFeature* AND cmdline:*-Online* AND cmdline:*-FeatureName*)) AND ((cmdline:*TelnetServer* OR cmdline:*Internet-Explorer-Optional-amd64* OR cmdline:*TFTP* OR cmdline:*SMB1Protocol* OR cmdline:*Client-ProjFS* OR cmdline:*Microsoft-Windows-Subsystem-Linux*)))
